  - mechanism elimination
abstract: >-
  A preregistered research program (14 hypotheses across H001–H011b, 53
  falsifiable sub-predictions) investigating whether Hodge decomposition improves graph
  neural network classification. Systematic mechanism elimination
  (sample size, feature density, graph topology) narrows the positive NCI1
  claim (+8.6 pp, p_BH = 4.83e-3) to an architecture-data complementarity
  interaction. Includes 497 tests, 100% coverage, and statistically
  defensible reporting (BCa bootstrap, paired Wilcoxon, BH-FDR).
